  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is projected from the ground with a kinetic energy $E$ at an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ with the horizontal. Its kinetic energy at the highest point of its motion will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YGPJE",
      "text": "$E / \\sqrt{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NfqgP",
      "text": "$E / 2$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "B3ump",
      "text": "$E / 4$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Zjvs3",
      "text": "$E / 8$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At ground, $E=\\frac{1}{2} m u^{2}$ \r\nAt highest point, $E^{\\prime}=\\frac{1}{2} m\\left(u \\cos 60^{\\circ}\\right)^{2}$\r\n$$\r\nE^{\\prime}=\\frac{E}{4}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
